// 26 U.S.C. Subtitle H — Financing of Presidential Election Campaigns
// (Chapter 95 §§9001-9013 Presidential Election Campaign Fund; Chapter 96
// §§9031-9042 Presidential Primary Matching Payment Account). The text is
// pinned whole (`sources.law`, generated from the shared Title 26 snapshot,
// `sync_us_irc_fragments.py --package election-funding`); modules below
// formalize it.
//
// MODULE MAP
//   package.law                  — shared ontology, imports, type aliases (this file)
//   01-general-election.law      — Chapter 95: party classification (§9002),
//                                  certification conditions (§9003),
//                                  entitlement computation (§9004),
//                                  certification (§9005), payments (§9006),
//                                  examinations/repayments (§9007)
//   02-primary-matching.law      — Chapter 96: eligibility (§9033),
//                                  entitlement/matching (§9034), expenditure
//                                  limitations (§9035), certification
//                                  (§9036), examinations/repayments (§9038)
//   03-fund-payments-and-conventions.law — stage 1b: §9005/§9036
//                                  certification duties+finality, §9006/
//                                  §9037 Fund/Account payment mechanics
//                                  (ported from us.irc.trust_funds' shape),
//                                  §9008 conventions (read in full: (a)-(h)
//                                  historical machinery, (i) the currently
//                                  operative 2014 termination/transfer rule)
//   04-audits-repayments-and-offenses.law — stage 1b: §9007(b)-(d)/§9038(b)-
//                                  (d) repayment determinations as Commission
//                                  powers, §9009/§9039 reports/rulemaking,
//                                  §9041 judicial review, §9012/§9042
//                                  criminal-penalty offense classification
//                                  (DECISION-0194 mental element, as
//                                  `us.irc.crimes` does)
//   05-general-election-stage3.law — stage 3: §9003(d) withdrawal, §9004(c)-(e)
//                                  use restriction and personal-funds
//                                  certification, §9007(a) audit duty, §9008
//                                  historical machinery ((b)(3)-(4), (c), (d)(4),
//                                  (e), (g)), §9009(b)/§9010 Commission powers
//   06-primary-matching-stage3.law — stage 3: §9033(c)(1)(A), (c)(2)-(4),
//                                  §9038(a) audit duty, §9038(b)(3) retention and
//                                  pro-rata repayment, §9039(b)/§9040(c)-(d)
//                                  Commission powers
//
// FECA (52 U.S.C., cited here under its former Title 2/26 U.S.C. cross-
// reference numbering as "section 315" etc.) and the Federal Election
// Commission's own procedures are EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES throughout — named,
// not reproduced. `us.irc.definitions` is a sibling package under
// construction; this stage does not depend on it.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.election_funding version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:election_funding:clir";

import us.irc.core version "0.1.1";

type Person = us.irc.core::Person;
type Organ = us.irc.core::Organ;
